The standalone Vast CLI is pinned to official signed tag v1.5.2, exact commit
bc7356483dd0f922ee17975c5357741f0d5d81fc. This release includes the upstream
fix that keeps API keys out of request URLs. The reviewed source digest, the
two-line isolated-interpreter patch digest, and every pure-Python wheel digest
are code-owned by deploy/inference-operator/vastai-offline-lock.json.
The installer never downloads or resolves packages. Boot admission verifies
the exact wheelhouse and every extracted imported file; runtime uses isolated
Python with no system or user site packages. Upstream update checks are disabled
in the admitted standalone source.

Dependency review performed 2026-08-20: official origin, signed tag, exact
artifact hashes, license, maintainer provenance, network/update behavior, and
the full five-package closure were checked. pip-audit reported no known
vulnerabilities in this reduced closure. The ordinary vastai 1.5.2 package was
explicitly rejected: its much larger pinned optional dependency graph included
known-vulnerable cryptography 49.0.0 and pillow 12.2.0 artifacts.
